tun:MECH-COR-01 a tun:FailureMechanism,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Corrosion" ;
    rdfs:comment "Corrosion of embedded reinforcing steel due to chloride ingress, carbonation, or moisture penetration, leading to expansion of corrosion products, cracking, delamination, and spalling of cover concrete" .

tun:MECH-COR-02 a tun:FailureMechanism,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Corrosion" ;
    rdfs:comment "Corrosion of steel or cast iron segmental liner plates and flanges, including through-corrosion of liner plate and galvanic corrosion at bolted connections due to dissimilar metal contact" .

tun:MECH-COR-03 a tun:FailureMechanism,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Corrosion" ;
    rdfs:comment "Corrosion and deterioration of ceiling hanger rods, clevises, turnbuckles, connection pins, and anchor connections in tunnel environment. Adhesive (chemical) anchors may lose capacity over time under sustained tension in overhead applications." .

tun:MECH-COR-ROCK-REINF-01 a tun:FailureMechanism,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Corrosion" ;
    rdfs:comment "Rock reinforcement elements (bolts, dowels, cables) deteriorate and lose strength due to corrosive tunnel environment and exposure. Rock fragments also become loose over time and drop onto roadway." .

tun:MECH-LEAK-01 a tun:FailureMechanism,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Leakage_Water" ;
    rdfs:comment "Groundwater intrusion through construction joints, liner gaskets, and full-depth cracks in the tunnel liner. May be aggravated by hydrostatic pressure, seasonal variation, and crack/joint movement." .

tun:MECH-STRUCT-CRACK-01 a tun:FailureMechanism,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Structural_Movement_Overload" ;
    rdfs:comment "Structural cracking due to stresses not accounted for in design (e.g., differential settlement, structural overload). Distinct from thermal/shrinkage cracks which are non-structural." .

